        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nThis is **not a duplicate**, but structurally it is close to Study 06.\n\nMore importantly, Lionel explicitly explains his own navigation method. He says there are different storylines, warns that his delivery jumps among many simultaneous issues, and says the material does not proceed as a simple ordered list. \n\nLater he announces a branch directly: `Let me jump to this subject and then jump back.` \n\nThat strongly validates **branch-and-return as a general Lionel live-navigation behavior**, rather than something peculiar to the political-realignment subject of Study 06.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
