        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 3 · Free Speech Master Thread\n## 5:46–10:29\n\nLionel states the broad thesis that attempts to stop Candace are ultimately part of an effort to restrict speech more generally. He uses controversial health advice as his example of speech he believes may be wrong or dangerous but should nevertheless remain speakable. \n\nHe then predicts that critics will connect Candace to Alex Jones and Sandy Hook as part of a future suppression argument. \n\n**Sequence function:** establish the master thread to which later case, history, and personality branches will attach.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
