        },
        "markdown": "# 4 · Alex Jones Suppression Scenario\n## 10:29–26:56\n\nLionel deliberately jumps away from the main thread, discusses commentators whose attitudes toward Candace surprise him, and predicts an escalation from rebutting her arguments to trying to remove her voice from public life. He describes this as turning `Alex Jones` into a verb. \n\nHe then develops Alex Jones as historical and legal precedent for the broader chilling-effect argument, connecting large civil judgments with the possible silencing of speakers. \n\n**Existing moves:** future scenario, historical precedent, system definition, pattern identification.\n\n**Validation:** Study 07's scenario move recurs immediately.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
