        },
        "markdown": "# 5 · Live Subject Enters the Room\n## 26:56–32:17\n\nDuring the stream Lionel is told that Candace Owens is watching. He acknowledges her presence, addresses her directly, praises her earlier program, and then continues discussing why she attracts unusually intense hostility. \n\nHe uses historical skepticism, disputed official narratives, family-memory examples, and the idea that history itself is continually contested to defend a culture of questioning. \n\n**Production observation:** a person who is already a major subject of the episode can become a live audience participant without changing formal host ownership.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
