        "markdown": "# 6 · Trial Reenactment and Proof Audit\n## 32:17–49:22\n\nLionel returns to the Tyler Robinson case and begins the familiar proof-oriented audit: did the defendant fire the alleged weapon, what connects him to it, what can actually be shown, and how persuasive would those claims be to jurors. \n\nHe then explicitly places himself in a defense-lawyer role and addresses an imagined jury, using the recurring lint-brush and bazooka comparisons to dramatize an object that he argues has not been linked to the crime. \n\nThe reenactment continues into the alleged confession and questions about hearsay, demeanor, and witness testimony. \n\n**Strong recurrence:** `Simulates Scenario -> role = juror-proof-test`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
