        "markdown": "# 7 · Storyline Registry and Research Network\n## 49:22–57:23\n\nLionel explicitly pauses the trial thread and says there are three parts: the whodunit or detective work, the trial, and another broader storyline. He describes Candace, Baron, and other researchers performing extremely deep dives and contrasts that distributed evidence work with opponents whom he portrays as offering mostly character judgments. \n\nHe also returns to the large incoming tip stream and asks why defense investigators would not seek potentially useful material from these researchers.  \n\n**Validation:** the information-network model from Study 06 recurs.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
