        "markdown": "# 8 · Historical Pattern and Hidden-System Branch\n## 57:23–1:03:02\n\nLionel brings in earlier controversies about the Warren Commission and other historical cases to argue that dismissing a theory because a cover-up would require many participants is not persuasive to him. \n\nHe then introduces his own catchall label for an uncertain hidden group responsible for wrongdoing, explicitly acknowledging that he does not know which specific institution or combination of institutions would compose it. \n\n**Function:** move from an observable dispute into a speculative system model while preserving at least some uncertainty about actor identity.",
