        "markdown": "# 9 · Performance and Persona Audit\n## 1:03:02–1:13:41\n\nLionel turns to Erica Kirk and TPUSA figures, interpreting public demeanor, grief performance, staged presentation, inconsistencies, and what he regards as tells. \n\nHe repeatedly mixes serious interpretation with comedy and explicitly says humor works because it exposes an absurd underlying premise. \n\n**Existing roles:** persona contrast, demeanor interpretation, coherence audit, humor-as-argument.\n\nNo new media-commentary family is required.",
