      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🪞 Self-Described Grammar\n\nStudy 08 provides unusually direct evidence about Lionel's own mental model of the show.\n\nHe says:\n\n- there are **different storylines**\n- many issues are occurring simultaneously\n- he **jumps around**\n- a simple ordered presentation does not match how he works\n- he may think of another subject while speaking\n- he can deliberately **jump to a subject and then jump back**\n\nThe relevant statements appear near the beginning and again around 10:29.  \n\nThis turns `branch-and-return` from an analyst's convenience into a **speaker-described production behavior**.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
