      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧵 Thread Model Refinement\n\nStudy 06 suggested a **Thread Stack** with one primary thread and temporary branches.\n\nStudy 08 shows something slightly richer: several **persistent peer storylines** can remain suspended at once.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- free speech and suppression\n- Tyler Robinson trial\n- whodunit research\n- TPUSA and Erica\n- Candace's influence\n- changing political alliances\n\nThe navigation model therefore may need:\n\n- `threadSet`\n- `activeThread`\n- `suspendedThreads`\n- `parentThread` when a true sub-branch exists\n- `returnPoint`\n- `threadPriority`\n- `branchTrigger`\n\nThis is a refinement of the navigation primitive, **not a new episode family**.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
