        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎭 Scenario Simulation Is Converging\n\nAcross the studies Lionel repeatedly constructs temporary worlds and performs roles inside them.\n\n## Already observed\n- imagined courtroom and juror test\n- reconstructed debate answer\n- projected future news cycle\n- proposed strategic countermove\n\n## Study 08 adds strong recurrence\n- extended defense-lawyer jury simulation\n- exaggerated opponent-expert roleplay\n\nThis increasingly supports one deeper operation:\n\n## `Lionel Simulates a Scenario`\n\nPossible roles:\n\n- `proof-test`\n- `future-projection`\n- `counterfactual-response`\n- `strategic-intervention`\n- `parodic-opponent-model`\n\nThis is ontology **compression**, not expansion.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
