        },
        "markdown": "# 👁️ Live Participant Presence\n\nA notable production event occurs when Lionel learns that Candace, already one of the episode's central subjects, is watching the live stream. He acknowledges her and temporarily addresses portions of the discussion directly to her. \n\nThis does not make her a formal guest.\n\nA lightweight production primitive may be enough:\n\n`Live Audience Presence`\n\nwith:\n\n- participant\n- detection time\n- source: chat or moderator\n- acknowledgment range\n- whether direct address follows\n\nKeep this provisional until another specimen uses it structurally.",
