      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-08"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📏 Confidence and Next Step\n\n## High confidence\n- this transcript is structurally distinct from the earlier specimens, not a duplicate\n- branch-and-return is likely a general Lionel live-navigation style\n- multiple top-level storylines can coexist without requiring separate episode templates\n- scenario simulation is becoming a deeper reusable operation\n- evidence audit and juror reenactment are stable Lionel behaviors\n- live chat is an input into navigation, not merely audience texture\n- the grammar is converging despite increasingly broad subject matter\n\n## Medium confidence\n- `threadSet` deserves explicit representation rather than derived metadata\n- `Live Audience Presence` deserves a production primitive\n- `Lionel Live Monologue` should replace more topic-specific names such as `Associative Realignment Monologue`\n\n## Study implication\nAnother one or two deliberately different specimens should now be enough to decide whether discovery can stop and reusable class design can begin.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786069297959,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    }
